---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content'
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { DIFFICULTY, EXTERNAL_RESOURCES, MANUAL_URL, SITE } from '../consts'

const showDrafts = import.meta.env.SHOW_DRAFTS === '1'
const modules = (await getCollection('modules', ({ data }) => showDrafts || !data.draft)).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
)
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Memorize the manual.</h1>
      <div class="prose mt-5">
        <p>
          <a href={MANUAL_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Keep Talking and Nobody Explodes</a> is
          a game about a bomb only one person can see and a manual only everyone else can read. It is
          at its best when the defuser is talking fast and the experts are flipping pages — and it
          gets a lot better when nobody has to flip pages at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          I memorized the manual. Not because it makes you win, but because the game turns into a
          different and better thing when the lookup disappears: you stop reading rules at each other
          and start actually communicating. A module that took forty seconds takes eight.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site is what I worked out along the way. One page per module, each with the specific
          tricks I used — where I chunked a table, which mnemonic stuck, what I got wrong for weeks
          before it clicked. Where it helps, there is a drill on the page to practice against.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>People memorize differently.</strong> Treat everything here as one worked example
          rather than the method. If my mnemonic for Who's on First does nothing for you, the useful
          part is the shape of it — a sentence whose first letters carry the list — not the sentence
          itself. Steal the structure, write your own words.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-4" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        The modules
      </h2>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2.5">
        {
          modules.map((m) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={`/modules/${m.id}/`}
                class="block h-full rounded-lg border p-3.5 transition-colors"
                style="border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-elev)"
              >
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                  <h3 class="font-medium">{m.data.title}</h3>
                  <span class="shrink-0 text-xs" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
                    {DIFFICULTY[m.data.difficulty].label}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-muted)">{m.data.summary}</p>
                {m.data.hasDrill && (
                  <span class="mt-2 inline-block text-xs" style="color: var(--color-amber)">
                    Has a drill
                  </span>
                )}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-4" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        Where to start
      </h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Go in difficulty order, not manual order. Simple Wires and The Button carry most of the
          early value because they come up constantly. Keypads and Simon Says are next — both are
          small tables that reward a single good mnemonic.
        </p>
        <p>
          Leave <a href="/modules/whos-on-first/">Who's on First</a> and{' '}
          <a href="/modules/wire-sequences/">Wire Sequences</a> for last. They are the two that take
          real time, and doing them first is how people bounce off this entirely.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-4" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        Other resources
      </h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5">
        {
          EXTERNAL_RESOURCES.map((r) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={r.href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                class="font-medium underline underline-offset-2"
                style="color: var(--color-amber)"
              >
                {r.label}
              </a>
              <span class="ml-1.5 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
                {r.note}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
        Comments, corrections or requests: <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}
          class="underline underline-offset-2"
          style="color: var(--color-amber)">{SITE.email}</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
